00:11:10.800 --> 00:11:12.600
So we have all
this together, all

00:11:12.600 --> 00:11:14.830
on a web browser-based system.

00:11:14.830 --> 00:11:17.680
It's very simple if you're
not a GIS expert to use.

00:11:17.680 --> 00:11:20.910
We can also bring in data
from our clients or data

00:11:20.910 --> 00:11:22.360
that's different than this.

00:11:22.360 --> 00:11:26.375
So we have it all together,
and one thing we've been--

00:11:30.000 --> 00:11:32.400
so one of the use
cases that's been great

00:11:32.400 --> 00:11:34.860
for us for helping
our clients has

00:11:34.860 --> 00:11:37.600
been like all these
natural disasters.

00:11:37.600 --> 00:11:40.890
So I actually was in
this room yesterday.

00:11:40.890 --> 00:11:44.940
I saw a talk by a
guy from Mayday.ai,

00:11:44.940 --> 00:11:46.920
and he said that
70% of the US is

00:11:46.920 --> 00:11:48.943
at risk for a natural disaster.

00:11:48.943 --> 00:11:50.610
So there are the fires
out here, there's

00:11:50.610 --> 00:11:52.380
the floods in the Midwest,
and there's the hurricanes

00:11:52.380 --> 00:11:52.920
out east.

00:11:55.440 --> 00:11:58.260
When we have a storm
like that, no one

00:11:58.260 --> 00:12:00.030
